# Install with:  crontab -e   (as the user that owns the project directory)
# Times use the system timezone — set it once: sudo timedatectl set-timezone Europe/Bratislava
# Adjust the path if the project is not in /home/pi/youtube-report-bot.
#
# Reporting weeks are Sunday–Saturday in Pacific time (REPORT_WEEK_END=saturday, DATA_LAG_DAYS=3).
# Saturday's data is lag-complete from Tuesday 00:00 Pacific = Tuesday 09:00 CET / CEST, so the
# report runs on Tuesday from 10:00. Every run from Tuesday to the following Monday (Pacific)
# selects the same week, so a retry can never produce a second, different report.

# Weekly report: every Tuesday at 10:00
0 10 * * 2 /home/pi/youtube-report-bot/deploy/pi/run_report.sh

# Retry at 14:00 in case the morning run failed. Same anchored week as the 10:00 run, so an
# already-sent week is skipped (duplicate guard per channel + period).
0 14 * * 2 /home/pi/youtube-report-bot/deploy/pi/run_report.sh

# Weekly SQLite backup: Tuesday at 15:00
0 15 * * 2 /home/pi/youtube-report-bot/deploy/pi/backup_db.sh >> /home/pi/youtube-report-bot/logs/cron.log 2>&1
